.TH COLDRUN 1 "" "coldrun" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
coldrun \- fetch, vet and sandbox any downloaded script in one command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coldrun
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fISOURCE\fR [\-\- \fISCRIPT ARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
coldrun fetches a script into quarantine, works out its language and
dependencies, vets the script and its dependencies, then runs it in a
sandbox with no network, no home directory and a read\-only root unless
you allow more. The sandbox is the protection; the scan is the warning.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "coldrun run SOURCE"
Fetch, vet, sandbox and run SOURCE. Everything after \-\- goes to the script.
.TP
.B \-\-net \fIVALUE\fR
Network policy inside the sandbox.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-host \fIVALUE\fR
Permit one HOST[:PORT]; repeatable; implies \-\-net allow.
.TP
.B \-\-listen \fIVALUE\fR
Forward [ADDR:]PORT into the sandbox for callbacks; ADDR defaults to 127.0.0.1. Give your VPN address (or 0.0.0.0) to accept from a target. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-rw \fIVALUE\fR
Mount one host path read\-write; repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-out \fIVALUE\fR
Where files the script writes are copied on exit.
.TP
.B \-\-backend \fIVALUE\fR
Force a sandbox backend: bwrap or podman.
.TP
.B \-\-lang \fIVALUE\fR
Override type detection.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation on medium risk.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Run despite a high\-risk verdict.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON document on stdout (docs/report.schema.json); human output goes to stderr.
.SS "coldrun scan SOURCE"
Vet SOURCE and print the findings and verdict without building a sandbox or running it.
.TP
.B \-\-lang \fIVALUE\fR
Override type detection.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON document on stdout (docs/report.schema.json); human output goes to stderr.
.SS "coldrun deps SOURCE"
Print the resolved dependencies of SOURCE without installing or running anything.
.TP
.B \-\-lang \fIVALUE\fR
Override type detection.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON document on stdout (docs/report.schema.json); human output goes to stderr.
.SS "coldrun doctor"
Check bwrap, podman, uv and kernel support, and say how to fix what is missing.
.SS "coldrun cache"
Manage cached dependency environments.
.TP
.B coldrun cache list
Show cached environments: key, runner, packages, size.
.TP
.B coldrun cache clean
Delete every cached environment.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The script's own exit code, except:
.TP
.B 2
usage error, or the source could not be fetched or recognised
.TP
.B 100
refused by vetting (high risk without \-\-force, or medium risk declined)
.TP
.B 101
the sandbox could not be set up; run \fBcoldrun doctor\fR
.TP
.B 102
dependencies could not be resolved or installed
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/coldrun/
quarantine directories and cached dependency environments
.TP
.I ~/.config/coldrun/config.toml
configuration
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bwrap (1),
.BR podman (1)
.PP
https://github.com/rj\-karan/coldrun
